 ### [Adaptive Density Control](9188-adaptive-density-control.md)
-Adaptive Density Control (ADC) is a dynamic optimization strategy used in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) to adjust the number and spatial distribution of Gaussian primitives during training. It solves the problem of sparse initial Structure-from-Motion (SfM) point clouds by adding, cloning, or removing primitives based on gradient magnitude, scale, and opacity. What sets it apart from its siblings is its reliance on view-space positional gradient magnitudes accumulated over visible iterations to trigger deterministic splitting, cloning, or pruning, rather than stochastic sampling or importance-weighted reweighting. See [Adaptive Density Control](9188-adaptive-density-control.md).
