 ### [Hyperparameter Settings](11076-hyperparameter-settings.md)
-Hyperparameter Settings define the numerical configuration for the optimization process, regularization terms, and learning rates required to stabilize the training of 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) and its variants. This method solves the problem of training instability and convergence failure, particularly in inverse rendering or sparse-view scenarios, by providing specific values for optimizer parameters, loss weights, and per-parameter learning rates. It is distinct from sibling methods like [Adaptive Density Control](9188-adaptive-density-control.md) because it does not dynamically adjust the primitive count but rather fixes the numerical constraints under which the densification and rendering operations occur. See [Hyperparameter Settings](11076-hyperparameter-settings.md).
