 ### [Densification and Splitting](13466-densification-and-splitting.md)
-This family manages the dynamic topology of 3D Gaussian primitives during training to balance reconstruction fidelity against computational cost. It solves the problem of under-representation (blurry regions) and over-representation (redundant primitives) by periodically splitting, cloning, or pruning Gaussians based on optimization metrics. It differs from static initialization methods by actively modifying the primitive set during the optimization loop, and from pure pruning strategies by including constructive operations (splitting/cloning) to increase density. See [Densification and Splitting](13466-densification-and-splitting.md).
